model {
  extend basalt.modelGateway {
    metadata {
      constraint "Runtime admission joins release-owned provider observations to a private trusted-start witness. A desired image binding or expected configuration hash is not evidence of the running image or its startup settings. The actual start callback retains the exact launch challenge and applied startup fingerprint before dispatch; authenticated readiness completes its boot. A failed witness write cannot start compute, and uncertain launch outcomes permit observation without a second start. Existing running compute may be preserved explicitly as unattested-active, never decoded as proven candidate evidence. Its adoption ACK and later passive readback derive the exact retained operation, manifest, decrypted capsule fingerprint, boot and committed selection from existing records. A fresh authenticated boot read and a selection recheck fence drift; capsule-only admission, another epoch, a candidate or draining slot, and an unknown ACK cannot authorize first-handoff advancement. Only a freshly joined attested candidate may pass promotion, with current controller, active selection and full positive and retired policy revisions still checked. The shared pool-runtime-attestation-v1 codec leaves existing slot and launch meanings unchanged. Private settings remain encrypted and stay out of receipts and logs. Ciphertext-corruption fixtures must change the decoded bytes and verify that precondition before expecting witness refusal; changing hex case alone is not corruption. Normal requests and explicit upkeep renew the selected runtime idle timer; synthetic probes and private health or witness reads never do. Legacy recovery cannot restart an admitted runtime, and initial adoption waits for any already admitted legacy restart to finish. The new runtime class stays unbound until separately admitted provisioning and activation."
    }
  }
}
